---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
import { securityUrl } from "../lib/site";
const items = [
  { icon: "HardDrive", title: "Local inspection", text: "Scans this computer and probes localhost. SSH connects to hosts you choose; desktop update checks use GitHub Releases. Project commands and SSH configuration can make their own network requests." },
  { icon: "EyeOff", title: "No product analytics", text: "No Holdmap account or product analytics. This site has no analytics scripts. Optional screen capture and agent activity recording start only when you choose them." },
  { icon: "KeyRound", title: "Credential redaction", text: "Recognized credentials in command displays are redacted; arbitrary positional secrets can be missed. Default scans do not open agent chats or settings. MCP &amp; skills inspection is explicit: bounded config files may contain credentials, whose values are excluded from results. Only allowed skill-header metadata is retained, not instructions. Activity recording excludes payload fields before retention." },
  { icon: "ShieldCheck", title: "Protected by default", text: "Hard protection cannot be overridden. Soft protection needs the CLI's explicit <code>--allow-protected</code> option or a desktop review that permits it. MCP refuses all protected targets." },
];
---
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="sec-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <span class="eyebrow">Security and privacy</span>
      <h2 class="h2" id="sec-title">It stops processes, <span class="soft">so it's careful.</span></h2>
      <p class="lede">Reviewed stop plans, process-identity checks and a restricted desktop webview. Restart history keeps raw commands needed to relaunch. Unix state uses private file permissions; Windows inherits the chosen folder's ACLs. Read the <a href={securityUrl}>security policy</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <ul class="cols" role="list">
      {items.map((i) => (
        <li>
          <Icon name={i.icon} size={16} />
          <h3>{i.title}</h3>
          <p set:html={i.text} />
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .lede a { color: var(--text-2); }
  .cols { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .cols li { padding: 32px 32px 0 0; }
  .cols li + li { padding-left: 32px; border-left: 1px solid var(--border); }
  li :global(svg) { color: var(--muted); }
  h3 { margin: 16px 0 8px; font-size: var(--fs-base); line-height: 24px; font-weight: 600; }
  li p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: var(--fs-md); line-height: 24px; }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .cols { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .cols li:nth-child(3) { padding-left: 0; border-left: 0; }
    .cols li:nth-child(n + 3) { margin-top: 32px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .cols { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); border-top: 0; }
    .cols li, .cols li + li { padding: 24px 0; border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); margin: 0; }
  }
</style>
